Nxe3 (11... Nxe5 12. Qe4 Qe7 13. Nd5 Ng4+ 14. Kg3 Qxe4 15. dxe4 Kd8 16. Rd1 $36) 12. Qxe3 Qh4+ 13. Ke2 Qb4 14. b3 O-O 15. Nf3 Bg4 $44 {Black has full compensation, but the position remains interesting.}) 8... Nxc4 9. Qd3 b5 $1 {[%csl Bb5] A key move - the only one for Black.} (9... Nxe5 $4 10. Qg3 $18 {[%cal Gg3e5,Gg3g7]}) 10. b3 c6 $1 {Another only move.} 11. bxc4 cxd5 12. cxd5 Qa5+ 13. Bd2 (13. c3 Ba6 $1 14. Nf3 O-O 15. Be3 b4 16. c4 Bxc4 17. Qxc4 Bxe3 18. Qb3 $13) 13... b4 14. Qb3 $13 {[%cal Gg1f3,Ge1c1] After Nf3 and O-O-O, it's an interesting three-result position, evaluated at +0.20 by the engine.}) 7... Nxc4 8. dxc4 c6 $1 {The strongest move, though quite difficult to find.} (8... Nxd5 9. cxd5 O-O 10. fxe5 c6 $1 (10... Bd4 $2 11. Nf3 Bg4 12. Bg5 Qe8 13. O-O-O Bxf3 14. gxf3 Bxb2+ 15. Kxb2 Qxe5+ 16. c3 Qxg5 17. e5 $16 {[%csl Bd5,Be5][%cal Gh1e1] White is better thanks to the powerful central pawns.}) 11. Be3 $5 (11. d6 Bd4 12. Nf3 Bxe5 13. Nxe5 Qa5+ $11 {[%csl Ba5,Bc6][%cal Ga5e5] This explains why 10...c6 is a strong inclusion.}) 11... Qh4+ $1 {The engine finds resources.} (11... Bxe3 $2 12. Qxe3 cxd5 13. O-O-O $16 {[%cal Ge4d5] exd5 will follow.}) 12. g3 Bb4+ $1 {An important resource.} (12... Qxe4 $4 {Not immediately.} 13. Bxc5 $18) 13. c3 Qxe4 14. Qf3 (14. Nf3 Bg4 $1 15. Rf1 Rfe8 16. cxb4 Rxe5 $13) 14... Qxe5 15. cxb4 Qxb2 16. Rd1 Qxb4+ 17. Bd2 Qc4 18. h3 $1 {[%cal Rc8g4] Preventing Bg4 is crucial.} cxd5 19. Ne2 $36 {[%cal Ge1f2] After Kf2, it's a complex position where White's chances are superior due to the extra knight's potential strength.}) 9. Nxf6+ Qxf6 10. f5 {[%cal Gg1f3]} g6 $1 {The only move, otherwise White consolidates with a huge advantage.} (10... O-O $2 11. Nf3 $18 {[%cal Gc1e3] Be3 will follow and win.}) 11. Nf3 gxf5 12. exf5 Bxf5 13. Be3 {Black must remain precise.} Bb4+ $1 {A strong positional move, aiming to force c3, which will make White's king less secure on the queenside.} (13... Bd6 14. O-O-O $36 {[%csl Bc1][%cal Gh1f1,Gf3h4,Gf1f8] White has numerous ideas along the f-file, and the king is safe.}) 14. c3 Bd6 15. O-O (15. O-O-O {[%csl Rc3]} Rg8 $13 {[%csl Rc1,Rc3]}) 15... Rg8 $1 {The only move.} 16. Nh4 $5 {This idea should be employed at some point.} Qxh4 17. Rxf5 $36 {[%csl Bg1][%cal Ga1f1] White maintains pressure on the f-file with a safely positioned king on g1.} *

