is strong move.} (10... Be7 $2 {looks logical, but it's a losing mistake.} 11. Nxf7 Rxf7 12. Bxf7+ Kxf7 13. e5 $18 {[%csl Rf7][%cal Ge1g1,Gd1h5]}) 11. dxc5 Qe7 $1 (11... dxc4 12. Qxd8 Rxd8 13. Nxc4 $14) 12. Qd4 dxc4 13. O-O-O Be6 14. Nd5 Nxd5 15. exd5 Qg5+ 16. Kb1 Rad8 17. d6 $36) 9. Qxf3 Be7 {[%csl Of6] Black has to protect Nf6.} (9... d6 $2 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. Qxf6 gxf6 12. Nd5 $16 {[%csl Bd5]}) 10. O-O d6 11. Bd4 {[%cal Gc3d5] we are ready for Nd5.} Be6 (11... c6 12. e5 $5 (12. a4 $36 {also fine.}) 12... dxe5 13. Bxe5 $36 {[%csl Be5,Rf7][%cal Gc3e4] Ne4 ideas, with some initiative.}) 12. Bb3 $36 {[%cal Ga1e1,Gg1h1] playable position with some initiative on the f-file. We can just continue with normal moves like Kh1-Rae1 and then see.}) (7... Na5 $5 {rare but interesting because it's connected to a beautiful idea on the next move.} 8. d4 Ba3 $3 $146 {strong idea that makes 7...Na5 playable.} (8... Bb4 $2 9. Bd3 $16) (8... Nxc4 $2 9. dxc5 d5 10. cxd6 cxd6 11. Qd4 $16 {[%cal Gf4g5] positional advantage.}) 9. bxa3 Nxc4 10. O-O {probably the best chance.} (10. e5 Nh5 $1 11. Bc1 d6 $13) 10... d5 $1 11. Bg5 dxe4 12. Nxe4 {Black still needs to be precise.} Bf5 $1 {only move.} 13. Bxf6 (13. Nxf6+ gxf6 14. Nh4 Bxc2 $1 15. Qxc2 fxg5 16. Qxc4 gxh4 $132) 13... gxf6 14. Qd3 Nb2 $1 {super move.} (14... Nd6 15. Nfd2 $36) 15. Nxf6+ Qxf6 16. Qb5 {[%csl Rb2,Rf5]} Bxc2 17. Qxb2 Bd3 18. Rfe1 $132 {equal but playable.}) 8. d4 $1 {the best chance.} (8. Qd2 {is White's most common continuation, but Black solves all the problems with} Be6 $11 {[%csl Be6]}) 8... Bb6 $1 {the best square.} (8... Bb4 {looks logical, but it's less strong.} 9. Bg5 $1 {[%csl Bg5] key idea.} Qe8 $1 (9... h6 $6 {most common move, but dubious.} 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. O-O {[%cal Gc3d5] Nd5 is a decisive idea.} Bxc3 {necessary exchange.} 12. bxc3 Qe7 13. Qe2 $14 {[%cal Ga1e1] White is better for sure.}) 10. Bxf6 (10. O-O $5 $146 Bxc3 11. bxc3 Nxe4 12. Qd3 Bf5 13. Rae1 Nxg5 14. Qxf5 Nxf3+ 15. Qxf3 Qd7 16. Re3 $44 {full compensation.}) 10... Qxe4+ 11. Kf2 Bxc3 12. bxc3 gxf6 13. Re1 $1 (13. Qd2 $6 {Amar-Ragnarsson, 2023.} Ne5 $1 $36 {[%csl Rc4]}) 13... Qf4 14. Bd3 {[%cal Ge1e4]} d5 15. g3 Qh6 16. Nh4 $36 {[%cal Gd1f3] great compensation and White's position is more pleasant to play for sure.}) 9. Bg5 {[%csl Bg5] this is always White's key idea. Now Black has two good continuations.} h6 {more common and natural.} (9... Bg4 {[%csl Rd4] only one game, but also good.} 10. Qd2 Bxf3 11. gxf3 Bxd4 12. h4 $1 $146 {[%csl Bg5] it's important to protect the bishop. White can continue with 0-0-0 next, and then attacking ideas on the kingside. 0.00 is the evaluation, but it's a new and very playable position.} (12. O-O-O $2 Bxc3 13. Qxc3 Nxe4 $1 $19 {[%csl Be4,Rg5] Bg5 is hanging.})) 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. Nd5 $1 Qg6 $1 {[%csl Re4,Rg2] important counterplay against e4.} (11... Qd8 $6 12. O-O $16 {[%csl Bd4,Be4][%cal Gc2c3] c3 next, and White is positionally better.}) 12. O-O Qxe4 $1 {Black must take the pawn; otherwise, his position is just worse.} (12... Bg4 {less precise.} 13. c3 Qxe4 14. Qd2 $36 {[%cal Ga1e1]}) 13. c3 {[%csl Bc3,Yd4] we should consolidate the d4 pawn.} Be6 $1 {[%csl Rd5] the best because it's direct.} (13... Bg4 14. Qd2 $36 {[%cal Ga1e1]}) 14. Nd2 $1 $146 Qh4 $1 {[%csl Bh4] only move.} (14... Qg6 $2 15. Nf4 $16 {[%csl Re6,Rg6]}) 15. Rf4 Qd8 $1 {The position is equal, but we have some interesting ideas.} (15... Qg5 $2 16. h4 Qd8 17. Nxb6 axb6 18. d5 $18 {[%csl Bh4][%cal Rd8g5] Black doesn't have the key Qg5 resource.}) 16. Nf6+ $5 (16. Nxb6 $2 {we don't win material because of} axb6 17. d5 Qg5 $19 {[%csl Bg5] key resource.}) (16. Ne4 {also interesting.} f5 $1 {[%csl Bf5] only move.} 17. Qe2 $5 (17. Ng3 Bxd5 18. Bxd5+ Kh8 $11 {[%cal Gf4f5] we can take back on f5, but it will be very little.}) 17... Bxd5 18. Bxd5+ Kh8 19. Raf1 $36 {for the engine this is equal, but over-the-board we have chances I feel.}) 16... Kh8 (16... gxf6 $4 17. Qh5 $18 {[%csl Rg8] Black is busted.}) 17. Qh5 Ne5 $1 